       DL Ensemble (all)       0.83 ± 0.02 0.96 ± 0.01 0.69 ± 0.04 0.95 ± 0.01\n","DL Ensemble (top3 by val AUC)       0.84 ± 0.02 0.95 ± 0.01 0.73 ± 0.04 0.95 ± 0.01\n","Confusion matrix, XGBoost-paper-full:  [[TN FP], [FN TP]] = [[99, 53], [7, 322]]\n","Confusion matrix, XGBoost-paper:  [[TN FP], [FN TP]] = [[99, 53], [7, 322]]\n","Confusion matrix, DL Ensemble (all):  [[TN FP], [FN TP]] = [[116, 36], [21, 308]]\n"]}],"source":["if RUN_B:\n","    show_cross(\"Poland\", \"Saudi\", \"4f-src\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7a022ad8","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022607,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.107239+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.084632+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Save the ML-style cross-dataset tables"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":67,"id":"fa0e3ed8","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.153203Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.152698Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.16219Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.161291Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.03389,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.163694+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.129804+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["saved ml_style_cross_dataset.csv\n"]}],"source":["if RUN_B:\n","    if CROSS_ML:\n","        pd.concat(CROSS_ML).to_csv(os.path.join(CFG[\"OUT_DIR\"], \"ml_style_cross_dataset.csv\"), index=False)\n","        print(\"saved ml_style_cross_dataset.csv\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"4f40db03","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022675,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.208732+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.186057+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Explainable AI (XAI): comparison of explanation methods, XGBoost vs the DL models (Part C)\n","\n","**Why this is not just \"SHAP plots\".** Most papers show one explanation method on one model and call it interpretability. Here the explanation methods are themselves\n","the object of study and are scored with measurable criteria, on the same children, the same fold models and the same reference distribution of \"absent\" features:\n","\n","| Criterion | What is measured | Ideal |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| **Recovery of the known rule** (NZ, Saudi) | Q-CHAT-10 labels follow \"sum of the 10 items >= T\". Per child, cosine similarity between the explanation and the **exact Shapley values of that rule** (computed by enumeration); share of importance on the 10 items; sign violations (an item answered \"concern\" should never push the risk down) | cosine 1, violations 0 |\n","| **Faithfulness** | Deletion / insertion test: remove (insert) features in the order the explanation ranks them and compare the change of the predicted-class probability with a random order | large gain |\n","| **Stability** | (i) same child, same model, explainer re-run with other random seeds / background rows; (ii) same child, model re-trained on other CV splits | cosine 1 |\n","| **Agreement** | between methods (same model) and between XGBoost and each DL model (same method) | descriptive |\n","| **Cost** | seconds per explained child | low |\n","\n","**Methods.** KernelSHAP (model-agnostic, all models), ExactSHAP (exact interventional Shapley values for XGBoost only: shap's TreeSHAP, or exhaustive enumeration of all 2^13 coalitions when shap cannot read the model; the same quantity; used to check our KernelSHAP), LIME (all models), Integrated Gradients (networks only;\n","averaged over baselines drawn from the same training rows as the SHAP background, so all methods share one definition of \"absent\"), permutation importance (global only, so it enters the\n","global-importance, rule-share and retrain-stability comparisons but not the per-child ones). All attributions are in units of change in P(ASD).\n","\n","**Models.** XGBoost-paper, MLP, MLP-PLE, TabPFN: re-fitted on the same folds with the same tuned parameters as Part A (their test AUC is printed so you can verify they match Part A).\n","\n","**What this does and does not show.** It ranks explanation *methods* by measurable quality in this screening setting and shows whether DL and XGBoost explain a child alike.\n","It does not prove that an explanation is clinically correct; sign checks on Poland are a plausibility check (the questionnaire is monotone by design), not ground truth.\n","Intervals are bootstrap CIs over the explained children (children of the same CV fold share a model, so they are slightly optimistic). There is deliberately **no composite score**: report the criteria separately."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"378446e0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.02162,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.252085+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.230465+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Libraries and availability of the explanation tools"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":68,"id":"4899d185","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.297457Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.296686Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.27251Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.27173Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.000462,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.274076+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:18.273614+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["shap / lime / captum available: True True True\n"]}],"source":["import itertools\n","from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n","\n","try:\n","    import shap\n","    HAS_SHAP = True\n","except Exception:\n","    HAS_SHAP = False\n","try:\n","    from lime.lime_tabular import LimeTabularExplainer\n","    HAS_LIME = True\n","except Exception:\n","    HAS_LIME = False\n","try:\n","    from captum.attr import IntegratedGradients\n","    HAS_CAPTUM = True\n","except Exception:\n","    HAS_CAPTUM = False\n","print(\"shap / lime / captum available:\", HAS_SHAP, HAS_LIME, HAS_CAPTUM)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8daba087","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023164,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.321261+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.298097+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Settings\n","Children explained per fold, background rows, sampling budgets and bootstrap sizes grow with the preset. `DLP_XAI_MODELS` / `DLP_XAI_DS` restrict the run (for example to leave out the slow TabPFN)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":69,"id":"dcdbff95","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.368456Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.367728Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.376703Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.376023Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.033506,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.378373+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.344867+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["XAI_PRESETS = {   # N_EXPLAIN = children explained per CV fold; BG = SHAP background rows; N_REP = CV repeats whose models are explained\n","    \"quick\":    dict(N_EXPLAIN=6,  BG=20, KS_N=120, LIME_N=300,  IG_STEPS=50,  IG_BASES=8, STAB_R=2, STAB_N=3, N_REP=1, DRAWS=4,  BOOT=300,  PERM_R=3),\n","    \"standard\": dict(N_EXPLAIN=20, BG=30, KS_N=200, LIME_N=600,  IG_STEPS=100, IG_BASES=16, STAB_R=3, STAB_N=5, N_REP=2, DRAWS=6,  BOOT=600,  PERM_R=5),\n","    \"full\":     dict(N_EXPLAIN=30, BG=50, KS_N=300, LIME_N=1000, IG_STEPS=200, IG_BASES=32, STAB_R=3, STAB_N=8, N_REP=3, DRAWS=10, BOOT=1000, PERM_R=10),\n","}\n","XCFG = dict(XAI_PRESETS[CFG[\"PRESET\"]])\n","XCFG[\"N_REP\"] = max(1, min(XCFG[\"N_REP\"], CFG[\"N_REPEATS\"]))\n","XCFG[\"EPS\"] = 0.01          # attributions smaller than 1 percentage point of probability are not counted as sign violations\n","XAI_MODELS = [m for m in os.environ.get(\"DLP_XAI_MODELS\", \"XGBoost-paper,MLP,MLP-PLE,TabPFN\").split(\",\") if m]\n","XAI_DS = [d for d in os.environ.get(\"DLP_XAI_DS\", \"Poland,NZ,Saudi\").split(\",\") if d in DS]\n","NF = len(BASE_FEATURES)\n","ITEM_IDX = list(range(10))\n","CAT_IDX = [i for i, f in enumerate(BASE_FEATURES) if f != \"age_months\"]\n","SHORT = [c.replace(\"_Score\", \"\").replace(\"age_months\", \"age\").replace(\"family_pdd\", \"family hx\") for c in BASE_FEATURES]\n","PER_CHILD = [\"KernelSHAP\", \"ExactSHAP\", \"LIME\", \"IG\"]       # methods that give one explanation per child\n","ALL_METHODS = PER_CHILD + [\"PERM\"]\n","MCOL = {\"KernelSHAP\": \"#0072B2\", \"ExactSHAP\": \"#56B4E9\", \"LIME\": \"#E69F00\", \"IG\": \"#009E73\", \"PERM\": \"#CC79A7\", \"RANDOM\": \"#767676\"}\n","MMARK = {\"KernelSHAP\": \"o\", \"ExactSHAP\": \"D\", \"LIME\": \"s\", \"IG\": \"^\", \"PERM\": \"v\", \"RANDOM\": \"x\"}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2bf93255","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.02235,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.423237+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.400887+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Prerequisite: Stage A tuned parameters and the known-rule check\n","On NZ and Saudi the label equals \"sum of the 10 items >= T\"; this is measured per dataset and the ground-truth test is enabled only when the agreement is at least 95%."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":70,"id":"68e277a2","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.469486Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.469235Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.485923Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.485065Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.041756,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.487691+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.445935+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Poland : label == (sum of items >= 3) for 86.9% of children -> not a rule dataset (sign check is only a plausibility check)\n","NZ     : label == (sum of items >= 4) for 100.0% of children -> known-rule ground truth ENABLED\n","Saudi  : label == (sum of items >= 4) for 100.0% of children -> known-rule ground truth ENABLED\n"]}],"source":["# the Stage A checkpoint (tuned hyper-parameters) is needed even when Part A is not run in this session\n","if \"CKPT\" not in globals():\n","    _cp = os.path.join(CFG[\"OUT_DIR\"], \"ckpt.pkl\")\n","    _imp = os.environ.get(\"DLP_CKPT_IMPORT\")\n","    if not os.path.exists(_cp) and _imp and CFG[\"PRESET\"] == \"full\" and os.path.exists(_imp):\n","        import shutil\n","        shutil.copy(_imp, _cp)\n","    CKPT = pickle.load(open(_cp, \"rb\")) if os.path.exists(_cp) else dict(rows={}, preds={}, tuned={})\n","    print(\"Stage A checkpoint:\", len(CKPT[\"rows\"]), \"finished runs,\", len(CKPT.get(\"tuned\", {})), \"tuned parameter sets\")\n","\n","\n","def rule_check(ds):\n","    \"\"\"Which threshold T makes 'sum of A1..A10 >= T' agree best with the label, and how often?\"\"\"\n","    X, y = DS[ds]\n","    items = X[QUESTION_COLS]\n","    ok = items.notna().all(axis=1).values\n","    sm, yy = items[ok].sum(axis=1).values, y[ok]\n","    T = max(range(1, 10), key=lambda t: np.mean((sm >= t) == yy))\n","    return T, float(np.mean((sm >= T) == yy))\n","\n","\n","RULE = {}\n","for _d in XAI_DS:\n","    _T, _a = rule_check(_d)\n","    RULE[_d] = dict(T=_T, agree=_a, use=_a >= 0.95)\n","    print(f\"{_d:7s}: label == (sum of items >= {_T}) for {100 * _a:.1f}% of children -> \"\n","          + (\"known-rule ground truth ENABLED\" if RULE[_d][\"use\"] else \"not a rule dataset (sign check is only a plausibility check)\"))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6e3616e6","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022798,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.534072+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.511274+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Helpers: choice of explained children, bootstrap and agreement statistics"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":71,"id":"b83513a8","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.582091Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.581329Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.594182Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.593434Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.039211,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.596165+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.556954+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def xai_children(ds):\n","    \"\"\"Children to explain (same for every model); a subset of them is re-explained under models from other CV repeats.\"\"\"\n","    X, y = DS[ds]\n","    n = min(len(y), XCFG[\"N_EXPLAIN\"] * CFG[\"N_SPLITS\"])\n","    ids = np.arange(len(y)) if n >= len(y) else train_test_split(np.arange(len(y)), train_size=n, stratify=y, random_state=CFG[\"SEED\"] + 11)[0]\n","    ids = np.sort(ids)\n","    rng = np.random.RandomState(CFG[\"SEED\"] + 12)\n","    stab = np.sort(rng.choice(ids, size=min(len(ids), XCFG[\"STAB_N\"] * CFG[\"N_SPLITS\"]), replace=False))\n","    return ids, stab\n","\n","\n","# ---- small numeric helpers ----\n","_trapz = getattr(np, \"trapezoid\", None) or np.trapz\n","\n","\n","def cos_rows(A, B):\n","    \"\"\"Per-row cosine similarity (nan if either vector is all zero).\"\"\"\n","    A, B = np.asarray(A, float), np.asarray(B, float)\n","    num, den = (A * B).sum(1), np.linalg.norm(A, axis=1) * np.linalg.norm(B, axis=1)\n","    return np.where(den > 0, num / np.where(den > 0, den, 1), np.nan)\n","\n","\n","def global_imp(A):\n","    g = np.abs(np.asarray(A, float)).mean(0)\n","    return g / g.sum() if g.sum() > 0 else g\n","\n","\n","def spearman_safe(a, b):\n","    a, b = np.asarray(a, float), np.asarray(b, float)\n","    return np.nan if (np.std(a) == 0 or np.std(b) == 0) else float(spearmanr(a, b)[0])\n","\n","\n","def boot_mean(v, B, seed=0):\n","    v = np.asarray(v, float)\n","    v = v[~np.isnan(v)]\n","    if len(v) == 0:\n","        return np.nan, np.nan, np.nan\n","    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n","    bm = v[rng.randint(0, len(v), (B, len(v)))].mean(1)\n","    return float(v.mean()), float(np.percentile(bm, 2.5)), float(np.percentile(bm, 97.5))\n","\n","\n","def paired_boot(a, b, B, seed=0):\n","    \"\"\"Paired difference a - b over children: mean, 95% CI, two-sided bootstrap p.\"\"\"\n","    a, b = np.asarray(a, float), np.asarray(b, float)\n","    ok = ~(np.isnan(a) | np.isnan(b))\n","    d = (a - b)[ok]\n","    if len(d) < 3:\n","        return np.nan, np.nan, np.nan, np.nan\n","    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n","    bm = d[rng.randint(0, len(d), (B, len(d)))].mean(1)\n","    p = max(2 * min((bm <= 0).mean(), (bm >= 0).mean()), 1.0 / B)\n","    return float(d.mean()), float(np.percentile(bm, 2.5)), float(np.percentile(bm, 97.5)), float(min(p, 1.0))\n","\n","\n","def fmt_ci(t, nd=3):\n","    return \"n/a\" if np.isnan(t[0]) else f\"{t[0]:.{nd}f} [{t[1]:.{nd}f}, {t[2]:.{nd}f}]\""]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"eca56a8a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022162,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.640923+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.618761+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Explanation methods (all in units of change in P(ASD))\n","### KernelSHAP"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":72,"id":"bd01c5ea","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.688682Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.687956Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.693553Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.692768Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.032118,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.69512+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.663002+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def _pf(model):\n","    \"\"\"Probability function used by every explainer: raw (un-scaled) features -> P(ASD) as a 1-D float array.\"\"\"\n","    return lambda X: np.asarray(model.predict_proba(np.asarray(X, dtype=\"float32\")), dtype=float).ravel()\n","\n","\n","def x_kernel_shap(pf, bg, Xex, nsamples, seed):\n","    \"\"\"KernelSHAP; l1_reg=False so that all 13 features get an attribution (recent shap versions otherwise keep only 10).\"\"\"\n","    np.random.seed(seed)\n","    expl = shap.KernelExplainer(pf, bg)\n","    phi = np.asarray(expl.shap_values(Xex, nsamples=nsamples, l1_reg=False, silent=True))\n","    if phi.ndim == 3:\n","        phi = phi[:, :, 0]\n","    return phi, float(np.ravel(expl.expected_value)[0])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"872af327","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.02221,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.739041+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.716831+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Exact Shapley values for XGBoost (TreeSHAP, with an exhaustive-enumeration fallback)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":73,"id":"e136c576","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.78662Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.78634Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.796021Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.795213Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.0362,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.797595+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.761395+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["_ALLM = ((np.arange(1 << NF)[:, None] >> np.arange(NF)) & 1).astype(bool)          # all 2^13 coalitions\n","_ALLPOP = _ALLM.sum(1)\n","_ALLW = np.array([math.factorial(s) * math.factorial(NF - 1 - s) / math.factorial(NF) for s in range(NF)])\n","\n","\n","def x_exact_shap(pf, bg, Xex):\n","    \"\"\"Exact interventional Shapley values by full enumeration of the 2^13 coalitions (value of a coalition = mean model output when\n","    the other features are taken from the background rows). Same definition and units as TreeSHAP / KernelSHAP, no library needed.\"\"\"\n","    out = np.zeros(Xex.shape)\n","    B = len(bg)\n","    for c, x in enumerate(Xex):\n","        Z = np.where(_ALLM[:, None, :], x[None, None, :], bg[None, :, :]).reshape(-1, NF).astype(\"float32\")\n","        v = pf(Z).reshape(len(_ALLM), B).mean(1)\n","        for i in range(NF):\n","            wo = np.where(~_ALLM[:, i])[0]\n","            out[c, i] = (_ALLW[_ALLPOP[wo]] * (v[wo + (1 << i)] - v[wo])).sum()\n","    return out\n","\n","\n","def x_tree_shap(xgb_model, bg, Xex, pf=None):\n","    \"\"\"Exact interventional TreeSHAP on the probability scale with the same background rows as KernelSHAP. Recent xgboost versions\n","    write split types that shap's TreeExplainer cannot read ('Categorical split is not yet supported'); in that case the identical\n","    quantity is obtained by exact enumeration (x_exact_shap), which is slower but needs no tree parser.\"\"\"\n","    try:\n","        expl = shap.TreeExplainer(xgb_model, data=bg, feature_perturbation=\"interventional\", model_output=\"probability\")\n","        phi = expl.shap_values(Xex, check_additivity=False)\n","        if isinstance(phi, list):\n","            phi = phi[-1]\n","        phi = np.asarray(phi)\n","        if phi.ndim == 3:\n","            phi = phi[:, :, -1]\n","        return phi\n","    except Exception as e:\n","        if pf is None:\n","            raise\n","        _warn_once((\"ts-fallback\",), f\"TreeSHAP unavailable ({type(e).__name__}); using exact enumeration of the 2^{NF} coalitions instead\")\n","        return x_exact_shap(pf, bg, Xex)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"809c253b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022036,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.841749+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.819713+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### LIME"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":74,"id":"f2cf8458","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.888772Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.888077Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.8942Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.893469Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.031292,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.895632+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.86434+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def x_lime(pf, Xtr, Xex, seed, n_samples):\n","    \"\"\"LIME (tabular, local linear surrogate). Binary features are categorical; the weight is the effect of the child's actual\n","    answer relative to answers sampled from the training data. Returns weights and the surrogate R^2.\"\"\"\n","    pf2 = lambda Z: np.column_stack([1 - pf(Z), pf(Z)])\n","    expl = LimeTabularExplainer(Xtr, feature_names=BASE_FEATURES, class_names=[\"non-ASD\", \"ASD\"], categorical_features=CAT_IDX,\n","                                discretize_continuous=False, mode=\"classification\", random_state=seed)\n","    W, R2 = np.zeros((len(Xex), NF)), np.zeros(len(Xex))\n","    for i, x in enumerate(Xex):\n","        e = expl.explain_instance(x, pf2, num_features=NF, num_samples=n_samples, labels=(1,))\n","        for j, w in e.local_exp[1]:\n","            W[i, j] = w\n","        sc = e.score\n","        R2[i] = sc[1] if isinstance(sc, dict) else sc\n","    return W, R2"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b74f600b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023812,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.942308+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.918496+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Integrated Gradients (networks only; baselines drawn from the SHAP background rows)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":75,"id":"72748ff1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.989925Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.989578Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.997689Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.99715Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.033653,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.998963+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:21.96531+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["class _EnsProb(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\"Mean of the sigmoid outputs of a seed ensemble of networks (what TorchModel.predict_proba returns).\"\"\"\n","    def __init__(self, nets):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.nets = nn.ModuleList(nets)\n","\n","    def forward(self, z):\n","        return torch.stack([torch.sigmoid(n(z)) for n in self.nets]).mean(0)\n","\n","\n","def ig_supported(model):\n","    return HAS_TORCH and HAS_CAPTUM and hasattr(model, \"nets\") and getattr(model, \"kind\", \"\") in (\"MLP\", \"MLP-PLE\", \"MLP-PLR\")\n","\n","\n","def x_ig(model, bg, Xex, steps, n_bases, seed):\n","    \"\"\"Integrated Gradients averaged over `n_bases` baselines drawn from the background rows (the same reference distribution as\n","    SHAP). Returns attributions and the mean absolute completeness error.\"\"\"\n","    fwd = _EnsProb(model.nets).to(DEVICE).eval()\n","    x = torch.tensor(model.scaler.transform(Xex), dtype=torch.float32, device=DEVICE)\n","    ig = IntegratedGradients(fwd)\n","    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n","    acc, dl = np.zeros(Xex.shape), []\n","    for _ in range(n_bases):\n","        b = torch.tensor(model.scaler.transform(bg[rng.randint(0, len(bg), len(Xex))]), dtype=torch.float32, device=DEVICE)\n","        a, d = ig.attribute(x.clone().requires_grad_(True), baselines=b, n_steps=steps, return_convergence_delta=True,\n","                            internal_batch_size=max(1, 8192 // steps))\n","        acc += a.detach().cpu().numpy()\n","        dl.append(np.abs(d.detach().cpu().numpy()))\n","    return acc / n_bases, np.mean(dl, 0)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e17f3133","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022861,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.044083+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.021222+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Permutation importance (global only)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":76,"id":"cda386f1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.089886Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.089517Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.094927Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.094306Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.030106,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.096481+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.066375+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def x_perm(pf, Xte, yte, repeats, seed):\n","    \"\"\"Global permutation importance on a held-out fold: mean increase of the Brier score when one feature is shuffled.\"\"\"\n","    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n","    base = brier_score_loss(yte, pf(Xte))\n","    blocks = []\n","    for j in range(NF):\n","        for _ in range(repeats):\n","            Xp = Xte.copy()\n","            Xp[:, j] = Xp[rng.permutation(len(Xp)), j]\n","            blocks.append(Xp)\n","    pr = pf(np.concatenate(blocks)).reshape(NF, repeats, len(Xte))\n","    return np.array([np.mean([brier_score_loss(yte, pr[j, r]) - base for r in range(repeats)]) for j in range(NF)])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6bc3e0a1","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022222,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.142769+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.120547+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Ground truth: exact Shapley values of the QCHAT-10 rule\n","Enumeration of all 2^10 coalitions of the 10 items gives the exact attribution of the rule \"label = 1 if sum >= T\"."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":77,"id":"12898d17","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.18922Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.188838Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.195519Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.194912Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.031295,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.196882+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.165587+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["_MASKS = ((np.arange(1024)[:, None] >> np.arange(10)) & 1).astype(float)\n","_POP = _MASKS.sum(1).astype(int)\n","_SHW = np.array([math.factorial(s) * math.factorial(9 - s) / math.factorial(10) for s in range(10)])\n","\n","\n","def rule_shapley(Xitems, Bitems, T):\n","    \"\"\"Exact interventional Shapley values (probability units) of the QCHAT rule f(x) = 1[sum(items) >= T] with the given\n","    background rows. Enumerates all 2^10 coalitions. Age / sex / family history play no role in the rule (attribution 0).\"\"\"\n","    out = np.zeros_like(Xitems, dtype=float)\n","    base_sum = (1 - _MASKS) @ Bitems.T                      # (1024, B): contribution of the background for absent items\n","    for c, x in enumerate(Xitems):\n","        v = ((_MASKS @ x[:, None] + base_sum) >= T).mean(1)   # value of every coalition\n","        for i in range(10):\n","            wo = np.where(_MASKS[:, i] == 0)[0]\n","            out[c, i] = (_SHW[_POP[wo]] * (v[wo + (1 << i)] - v[wo])).sum()\n","    return out"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2a6bb1ff","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.021623,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.241479+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.219856+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Faithfulness test: deletion and insertion curves"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":78,"id":"fb4facaf","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.28819Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.28774Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.297345Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.296713Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.035124,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.298824+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.2637+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def x_fidelity(pf, Xex, attrs, Xref, seed, draws):\n","    \"\"\"Deletion / insertion curves. Deletion: features are replaced by values of random training children, most supportive\n","    first (supportive of the class the model predicts). Insertion: start from a random training child and insert the child's own\n","    values in the same order. Both are averaged over `draws` random reference children (shared by all methods) and compared with\n","    a random feature order. Returns {method: dict(del_auc, ins_auc, del_curve, ins_curve)} (per child).\"\"\"\n","    n, F = Xex.shape\n","    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n","    refs = Xref[rng.randint(0, len(Xref), size=(draws, n))]\n","    p0 = pf(Xex)\n","    pred1 = p0 >= 0.5\n","    sgn = np.where(pred1, 1.0, -1.0)[:, None]\n","    orders = {m: np.argsort(-(np.asarray(A, float) * sgn), axis=1, kind=\"stable\") for m, A in attrs.items()}\n","    orders[\"RANDOM\"] = np.stack([rng.permutation(F) for _ in range(n)])\n","    rows = np.arange(n)[:, None]\n","    out = {}\n","    for m, order in orders.items():\n","        dele, ins = np.zeros((n, F + 1)), np.zeros((n, F + 1))\n","        for d in range(draws):\n","            Xd = np.empty((F + 1, n, F), dtype=\"float32\")\n","            Xi = np.empty((F + 1, n, F), dtype=\"float32\")\n","            for k in range(F + 1):\n","                a, b = Xex.copy(), refs[d].copy()\n","                if k:\n","                    cols = order[:, :k]\n","                    a[rows, cols] = refs[d][rows, cols]\n","                    b[rows, cols] = Xex[rows, cols]\n","                Xd[k], Xi[k] = a, b\n","            pr = pf(np.concatenate([Xd.reshape(-1, F), Xi.reshape(-1, F)]))\n","            half = (F + 1) * n\n","            q_d, q_i = pr[:half].reshape(F + 1, n), pr[half:].reshape(F + 1, n)\n","            dele += np.where(pred1[None, :], q_d, 1 - q_d).T\n","            ins += np.where(pred1[None, :], q_i, 1 - q_i).T\n","        dele, ins = dele / draws, ins / draws\n","        out[m] = dict(del_auc=_trapz(dele, axis=1) / F, ins_auc=_trapz(ins, axis=1) / F, del_curve=dele, ins_curve=ins)\n","    return out"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b86999f3","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022179,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.343694+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.321515+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Run: re-fit the Part A models, explain, score\n","### Checkpoint of the explanations\n","Results are saved after every finished dataset / model pair, so a stopped run resumes there."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":79,"id":"018b3aff","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.389483Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.389117Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.395148Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.394528Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.030979,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.396722+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.365743+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["XAI_CKPT = os.path.join(CFG[\"OUT_DIR\"], \"xai_ckpt.pkl\")\n","XRES = {}\n","if os.path.exists(XAI_CKPT):\n","    _old = pickle.load(open(XAI_CKPT, \"rb\"))\n","    if _old.get(\"meta\") == dict(preset=CFG[\"PRESET\"], xcfg=XCFG, seed=CFG[\"SEED\"]):\n","        XRES = _old\n","        print(\"resumed XAI checkpoint:\", [k for k in XRES if k != \"meta\"])\n","    else:\n","        print(\"XAI checkpoint belongs to another preset / configuration -> ignored\")\n","XRES[\"meta\"] = dict(preset=CFG[\"PRESET\"], xcfg=XCFG, seed=CFG[\"SEED\"])\n","_WARNED = set()\n","\n","\n","def _warn_once(key, msg):\n","    if key not in _WARNED:\n","        _WARNED.add(key)\n","        print(\"   [\" + msg + \"]\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"521146a8","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022358,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.442443+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.420085+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Re-fit the Part A models fold by fold (same splits, same tuned parameters)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":80,"id":"7bbd5095","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.489662Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.489291Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.497639Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.496927Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.034241,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.499247+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.465006+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def xai_params(ds, model, fold, Xb, yb, Xva, yva, seed):\n","    if model in (\"XGBoost-paper\", \"TabPFN\"):\n","        return {}\n","    p = CKPT.get(\"tuned\", {}).get((ds, \"13f\", model, fold))\n","    if p is None:\n","        _warn_once((\"tune\", ds, model), f\"no Stage A tuned parameters for {ds}/{model}: tuning here instead (results will differ slightly from Part A)\")\n","        p = tune_params(model, ds, Xb, yb, Xva, yva, seed)\n","    return p\n","\n","\n","def xai_fit_fold(ds, model, rep, fold):\n","    X, y = DS[ds]\n","    sp = SPLITS[ds][rep * CFG[\"N_SPLITS\"] + fold]\n","    assert sp[\"rep\"] == rep and sp[\"fold\"] == fold\n","    seed = CFG[\"SEED\"] + 1000 * rep + fold                      # identical to the Stage A seed of this fold\n","    tr, te = np.asarray(sp[\"train\"]), np.asarray(sp[\"test\"])\n","    imp = SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\").fit(X.iloc[tr])\n","    Xtr = pd.DataFrame(imp.transform(X.iloc[tr]), columns=BASE_FEATURES)\n","    ytr = y[tr]\n","    a, b = inner_split(ytr, seed)\n","    Xfit, yfit = Xtr.iloc[a].values.astype(\"float32\"), ytr[a]\n","    Xva, yva = Xtr.iloc[b].values.astype(\"float32\"), ytr[b]\n","    Xb, yb = balance(Xfit, yfit, seed)\n","    params = xai_params(ds, model, fold, Xb, yb, Xva, yva, seed)\n","    m = make_model(model, params, seed, ds, CFG[\"ENS_SEEDS\"]).fit(Xb, yb, Xva, yva)\n","    Xte = imp.transform(X.iloc[te]).astype(\"float32\")\n","    return m, dict(imp=imp, Xfit=Xb, te=te, Xte=Xte, yte=y[te], seed=seed)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9093b713","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022483,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.543547+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.521064+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Run all methods for one model on one set of children"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":81,"id":"c97566cf","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.589519Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.588832Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.59778Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.597042Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.03386,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.59927+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.56541+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def xai_run_methods(model, name, Xfit, Xex, seed):\n","    \"\"\"All per-child explanation methods for one model on one set of children. Returns (attr, seconds, diagnostics, background).\"\"\"\n","    pf = _pf(model)\n","    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n","    bg = Xfit[rng.choice(len(Xfit), min(XCFG[\"BG\"], len(Xfit)), replace=False)]\n","    attr, sec, diag = {}, {}, {}\n","    if HAS_SHAP:\n","        try:\n","            t0 = time.perf_counter()\n","            phi, base = x_kernel_shap(pf, bg, Xex, XCFG[\"KS_N\"], seed)\n","            sec[\"KernelSHAP\"], attr[\"KernelSHAP\"] = time.perf_counter() - t0, phi\n","            diag[\"KernelSHAP\"] = np.abs(phi.sum(1) + base - pf(Xex))\n","        except Exception as e:\n","            _warn_once((\"ks\", name), f\"KernelSHAP failed for {name}: {type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:100]}\")\n","        if name == \"XGBoost-paper\" and hasattr(model, \"m\"):\n","            try:\n","                t0 = time.perf_counter()\n","                attr[\"ExactSHAP\"] = x_tree_shap(model.m, bg, Xex, pf)\n","                sec[\"ExactSHAP\"] = time.perf_counter() - t0\n","            except Exception as e:\n","                _warn_once((\"ts\", name), f\"ExactSHAP failed: {type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:100]}\")\n","    if HAS_LIME:\n","        try:\n","            t0 = time.perf_counter()\n","            W, R2 = x_lime(pf, Xfit, Xex, seed, XCFG[\"LIME_N\"])\n","            sec[\"LIME\"], attr[\"LIME\"], diag[\"LIME\"] = time.perf_counter() - t0, W, R2\n","        except Exception as e:\n","            _warn_once((\"lime\", name), f\"LIME failed for {name}: {type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:100]}\")\n","    if ig_supported(model):\n","        try:\n","            t0 = time.perf_counter()\n","            G, dlt = x_ig(model, bg, Xex, XCFG[\"IG_STEPS\"], XCFG[\"IG_BASES\"], seed)\n","            sec[\"IG\"], attr[\"IG\"], diag[\"IG\"] = time.perf_counter() - t0, G, dlt\n","        except Exception as e:\n","            _warn_once((\"ig\", name), f\"Integrated Gradients failed for {name}: {type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:100]}\")\n","    return attr, sec, diag, bg"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"92d7eb1a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022751,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.645179+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.622428+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### One dataset x model: explanations, fidelity, stability and permutation importance"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":82,"id":"e54e2047","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.691339Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.690834Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.7066Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.706044Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.040085,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.707921+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.667836+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def xai_run(ds, name):\n","    t_all = time.time()\n","    X, y = DS[ds]\n","    ids, stab_ids = xai_children(ds)\n","    pos = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(ids)}\n","    n = len(ids)\n","    nan = lambda: np.full((n, NF), np.nan)\n","    rec = dict(ids=ids, stab_ids=stab_ids, y=y[ids], X=np.full((n, NF), np.nan), p={r: np.full(n, np.nan) for r in range(XCFG[\"N_REP\"])},\n","               attr={r: {} for r in range(XCFG[\"N_REP\"])}, perm={r: [] for r in range(XCFG[\"N_REP\"])}, auc=[],\n","               sec={}, diag={}, samp={}, fid={}, oracle=np.full((n, NF), np.nan), bg_items=None)\n","    for rep in range(XCFG[\"N_REP\"]):\n","        for fold in range(CFG[\"N_SPLITS\"]):\n","            m, info = xai_fit_fold(ds, name, rep, fold)\n","            pf = _pf(m)\n","            want = ids if rep == 0 else stab_ids\n","            te_set = set(info[\"te\"].tolist())\n","            mine = np.array([c for c in want if c in te_set], dtype=int)\n","            rec[\"auc\"].append(dict(rep=rep, fold=fold, auc=float(roc_auc_score(info[\"yte\"], pf(info[\"Xte\"])))))\n","            rec[\"perm\"][rep].append(x_perm(pf, info[\"Xte\"], info[\"yte\"], XCFG[\"PERM_R\"], info[\"seed\"]))\n","            if len(mine) == 0:\n","                continue\n","            Xex = info[\"imp\"].transform(X.iloc[mine]).astype(\"float32\")\n","            ii = np.array([pos[c] for c in mine])\n","            rec[\"p\"][rep][ii] = pf(Xex)\n","            if rep == 0:\n","                rec[\"X\"][ii] = Xex\n","            attr, sec, diag, bg = xai_run_methods(m, name, info[\"Xfit\"], Xex, info[\"seed\"])\n","            for meth, A in attr.items():\n","                rec[\"attr\"][rep].setdefault(meth, nan())[ii] = A\n","            if rep == 0:\n","                for meth, s in sec.items():\n","                    rec[\"sec\"].setdefault(meth, []).append((s, len(mine)))\n","                for meth, d in diag.items():\n","                    rec[\"diag\"].setdefault(meth, []).append(np.asarray(d))\n","                # faithfulness (deletion / insertion) against a random order, same references for all methods\n","                fid = x_fidelity(pf, Xex, attr, info[\"Xfit\"], info[\"seed\"] + 7, XCFG[\"DRAWS\"])\n","                for meth, d in fid.items():\n","                    slot = rec[\"fid\"].setdefault(meth, dict(del_auc=np.full(n, np.nan), ins_auc=np.full(n, np.nan),\n","                                                            del_curve=np.full((n, NF + 1), np.nan), ins_curve=np.full((n, NF + 1), np.nan)))\n","                    slot[\"del_auc\"][ii], slot[\"ins_auc\"][ii] = d[\"del_auc\"], d[\"ins_auc\"]\n","                    slot[\"del_curve\"][ii], slot[\"ins_curve\"][ii] = d[\"del_curve\"], d[\"ins_curve\"]\n","                # exact Shapley values of the QCHAT rule (NZ / Saudi only), with this fold's background rows\n","                if RULE.get(ds, {}).get(\"use\"):\n","                    rec[\"oracle\"][ii, :10] = rule_shapley(Xex[:, :10].astype(float), bg[:, :10].astype(float), RULE[ds][\"T\"])\n","                    rec[\"oracle\"][ii, 10:] = 0.0\n","                # sampling stability: re-run the stochastic explainers with other seeds / background rows on a few children\n","                k = min(XCFG[\"STAB_N\"], len(mine))\n","                reruns = [xai_run_methods(m, name, info[\"Xfit\"], Xex[:k], info[\"seed\"] + 100 * (r + 1))[0] for r in range(XCFG[\"STAB_R\"] - 1)]\n","                for meth in attr:\n","                    runs = [attr[meth][:k]] + [rr[meth] for rr in reruns if meth in rr]\n","                    if len(runs) >= 2:\n","                        cs = [cos_rows(runs[a], runs[b]) for a, b in itertools.combinations(range(len(runs)), 2)]\n","                        rec[\"samp\"].setdefault(meth, []).extend(np.nanmean(cs, 0).tolist())\n","            print(f\"   {ds}/{name} repeat {rep + 1}/{XCFG['N_REP']} fold {fold + 1}/{CFG['N_SPLITS']}: explained {len(mine)} children \"\n","                  f\"({time.time() - t_all:.0f}s)\")\n","    rec[\"runtime_total\"] = time.time() - t_all\n","    return rec"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a0fe3219","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023043,"end_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.752563+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-18T11:52:22.72952+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Run the explanations for every dataset and model (slow